    "path": "Prompt.md",
    "content": "Act as my senior .NET architect and interview coach.\n\nRead every interview question from `Interview_Question.md` in the original order.\n\none request use simple language for every section which can easuly understand\n\nFor each question, create a clear, practical answer using this exact structure:\n\n\n1. What is it?\n\n   * Define the concept in simple, human language. \n\n2. Why is it important?\n\n   * Explain the problem it solves.\n   * Explain why developers or architects need it in real projects.\n\n3. How does it work?\n\n   * Explain the internal working or execution flow.\n   * Avoid unnecessary theory.\n\n4. Practical example\n\n   * Give one realistic example from a banking, payment, authentication, or distributed system.\n\n5. Scenario-based interview answer\n\n   * Create a realistic interview scenario related to the question.\n   * Provide a natural answer that an experienced senior developer could speak during an interview.\n   * Use Problem → Decision → Implementation → Result when appropriate.\n\n6. Code example\n\n   * Provide a concise C#/.NET example when relevant.\n   * Explain the important parts of the code.\n   * Do not add code when it does not help explain the concept.\n\n7. Common mistakes\n\n   * Mention important implementation or production mistakes.\n\n8. Follow-up interview questions\n\n   * Provide 2–3 likely follow-up questions with short answers.\n\nInstructions:\n\n* Read the formatting and answer requirements from `Prompt.md`.\n* Answer every question in `Interview_Question.md`.\n* Do not skip, combine, duplicate, or reorder questions.\n* Preserve the original question number and title.\n* Organize answers into separate folders based on technology, such as:\n\n  * CSharp\n  * DotNet\n  * ASP.NET-Core\n  * Database\n  * Microservices\n  * Architecture\n  * Security\n  * Azure\n  * React\n  * Angular\n  * DevOps\n* Create a separate Markdown file for every question.\n* Use filenames in this format:\n  `QuestionNumber_Question_Title.md`\n* Save all generated files inside the `Interview_Answers` folder.\n* Before starting, verify that `Interview_Question.md` and `Prompt.md` exist.\n* Do not overwrite an existing complete answer.\n* If an existing answer is incomplete, complete it using the required structure.\n* Use clear, conversational English suitable for interview revision.\n* Make answers appropriate for a senior .NET full-stack developer with approximately 13 years of experience.\n* Correct any incorrect assumption in a question instead of agreeing with it.\n* Use practical explanations instead of generic or AI-sounding content.\n* Continue automatically until every question has been completed.\n"
