    "path": "Angular/Angular-Detailed-Chunk-15-Angular14-to-22-Migration-Part2/README.md",
    "content": "# Angular Interview Guide — Chunk 15\n\n## Angular 14 to Angular 22 Migration — Part 2\n\n- [142. How Would You Migrate Structural Directives to Built-in Control Flow and Validate Rendering Behavior?](142-control-flow-migration-validation.md)\n- [143. How Would You Plan a Low-Risk Migration from Angular 14 to Angular 22?](143-low-risk-migration-plan.md)\n- [144. How Would You Use Angular Update Schematics While Keeping Each Migration Commit Reviewable and Reversible?](144-reviewable-reversible-schematics.md)\n- [145. What Would You Check for Node.js, TypeScript, RxJS, Angular Material, and Third-Party Compatibility at Each Step?](145-toolchain-and-library-compatibility.md)\n- [146. Why Should Angular Major Versions Normally Be Upgraded Sequentially with ng update?](146-why-sequential-major-upgrades.md)\n- [147. Would You Upgrade Framework Versions and Rewrite the Application to Signals and Standalone Components at the Same Time? Explain the Trade-off.](147-upgrade-vs-rewrite-tradeoff.md)\n\nEvery question is contained in a separate detailed Markdown file.\n"
